      m_Calls: []
  m_text: ' From 1968 through 1991, bathtub racing became one of Southern Polytechnic
    State University''s memorable student traditions. Student teams constructed racing
    vehicles using cast-iron bathtubs, lightweight engines, and their own engineering
    creativity.



    The races brought students, faculty, alumni, spectators, and
    sponsors together around a uniquely Southern Poly combination of engineering,
    competition, creativity, and school spirit.



    The Southern Bathtub Racing
    Game preserves that tradition through an interactive recreation of the event
    and the SPSU campus. '
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
  m_fontAsset: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8f586378b4e144a9851e7b34d9b748ee, type: 2}
